config SERVICE_MIC_MANAGER
    bool "Microphone manager"
    depends on MIC
    default y
    help
      Arbitrates the microphone between dictation and app streaming.

if SERVICE_MIC_MANAGER

config SERVICE_MIC_MANAGER_QUEUE_MAX_MS
    int "Longest microphone queue, in milliseconds"
    range 32 320
    default 320
    help
      The queue between the microphone and its clients takes this much of
      samples when the heap has room for it beside what the Bluetooth
      packets carrying the audio need. A board with a small kernel heap
      keeps it shorter, leaving the packets more.

config SERVICE_MIC_MANAGER_QUEUE_MIN_MS
    int "Shortest microphone queue, in milliseconds"
    range 32 320
    default 128
    help
      The queue between the microphone and its clients takes less than its
      longest, in 32 ms steps, down to this when the heap is short.
      Below it, the microphone does not start. A short queue drops samples
      while Bluetooth stalls, which degrades transcription, but lets a board
      with a small kernel heap record at all.

module = SERVICE_MIC_MANAGER
module-str = Mic manager
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif
